abstract: >-
  The a-priori estimate M'(t) ≤ C − k M(t)² for the vorticity sup-norm of 3D incompressible
  Navier–Stokes on the torus is false when C, k depend only on the viscosity (explicit
  trigonometric counterexample) or on the viscosity and the energy (scaled localized vortex).
  With data-dependent constants it is equivalent to global regularity and remains open; no
  Clay Millennium Problem claim is made. Includes a Lean 4 audit of the symplectic-tether draft.
